From 1720fdeec6697f2119ff6dbf25f35e984f46ea95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: womarchy <womarchy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:51:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] glapi: expose EXT_external_objects entry points on OpenGL
 ES 3.0

EXT_memory_object, EXT_semaphore and their _fd variants require only
OpenGL ES 3.0 (EXT_semaphore even ES 2.0), and st/mesa advertises them on
any ES2 context whose driver has the memobj cap. The dispatch XML however
declared their functions es2="3.2", so on a driver that tops out at ES 3.0
or 3.1 (e.g. d3d12 on WSL: "OpenGL ES 3.0") the extension string lists
GL_EXT_memory_object_fd but glCreateMemoryObjectsEXT & co. are not in the
dispatch table and raise GL_INVALID_OPERATION.

Declare them es2="3.0", matching the extensions' requirements.

Found with a cross-process test on WSL: a Vulkan (dzn) image exported with
VK_KHR_external_memory_fd imports into a GLES 3.0 context only with this
change (300/300 correct 1080p frames; 0/300 without it).

